<div class="landing landing-home">
  <div class="home-top">
    <.marketing_nav current_user={assigns[:current_user]} />

    <section class="home-hero home-hero-compact">
      <div class="home-wrap">
        <p class="home-eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Terms of service</h1>
        <p class="home-lede">Last updated 12 October 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="home-band">
    <div class="home-wrap">
      <div class="legal">
        <p>
          These terms apply to the hosted Masthead service at masthead.site, including the
          dashboard, the marketplace and the sites it hosts. By creating an account you agree to
          them. How we handle personal data is described in the <.link navigate={~p"/privacy"}>privacy policy</.link>.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who provides Masthead</h2>
        <p>
          Masthead is provided by <strong>Dijkstra Software</strong>, a sole proprietorship
          registered in the Netherlands with the Chamber of Commerce (KvK) under number
          97259993. Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@masthead.site">hello@masthead.site</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Masthead software is open source under the MIT license. These terms cover the
          service we run, not your use of the source code, which the MIT license governs.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Your account</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You must be at least 16 years old to create an account.</li>
          <li>
            Give a working email address and confirm it. Accounts that aren't confirmed within
            30 days are suspended until they are.
          </li>
          <li>
            Keep your password and sign-in methods secure. You are responsible for what
            happens under your account, including what collaborators you invite do on your
            sites.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Free sites and site licenses</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Every site starts on the free plan, which has no time limit.</li>
          <li>
            A site license is per site and adds paid features such as a custom domain,
            collaborators and visitor statistics. Current prices are on the <.link navigate={
              ~p"/pricing"
            }>pricing page</.link>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Licenses are billed in advance, monthly or yearly, through Stripe, and renew
            automatically until you cancel.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can cancel at any time. The site stays licensed until the end of the period you
            paid for and then returns to the free plan; your content is not affected.
          </li>
          <li>
            Payments are not refunded, also not for a partly used period. This doesn't limit
            any rights you have by law as a consumer.
          </li>
          <li>
            We announce price changes at least 30 days before they apply to your next billing
            period.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Your content</h2>
        <p>
          You keep all rights to the content, uploads and themes you put on Masthead. You give
          us permission to store, process and publish them only as far as needed to run your
          sites and the service. You confirm that you have the rights to everything you upload.
        </p>
        <p>
          You are responsible for your sites, including complying with the law that applies to
          them, such as privacy rules for any personal data you publish or collect on them.
        </p>

        <h2>5. What isn't allowed</h2>
        <p>Don't use Masthead to publish, host or send:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>anything illegal, including content that infringes someone else's rights;</li>
          <li>malware, phishing, or sites that impersonate others;</li>
          <li>spam or unsolicited bulk messages;</li>
          <li>content that sexually exploits minors, or that threatens or harasses people;</li>
          <li>attempts to break, overload or get around the security of the service or the
            sandbox that themes run in.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To report content on a Masthead site that you believe is illegal, email
          <a href="mailto:hello@masthead.site">hello@masthead.site</a>
          with the address of the
          page and why. We review every report and tell you what we decided.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a site or account breaks these terms, we may take the content offline, suspend the
          site or close the account. Where we can, we warn you first and explain why.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Themes and the marketplace</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Only upload themes you have the right to distribute.</li>
          <li>
            By publishing a theme to the marketplace, you allow every Masthead user to install
            and use it on their Masthead sites.
          </li>
          <li>
            We may remove a theme from the marketplace if it breaks these terms or doesn't work.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Custom domains</h2>
        <p>
          You may only connect domains you control. You remain responsible for the domain's
          registration and DNS; we provision the TLS certificate once ownership is verified.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
          We work to keep Masthead available and your data safe, but the service is provided as
          is, without a guaranteed uptime. Keep your own copies of content you can't afford to
          lose. We may change or remove features; if a change takes away something you pay
          for, we tell you in advance.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Liability</h2>
        <p>
          Our total liability to you is limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months
          before the event that caused the damage. We are not liable for indirect damage such
          as lost profit or lost data. These limits don't apply to damage caused by our intent
          or gross negligence, or where the law doesn't allow them.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Ending your account</h2>
        <p>
          You can stop using Masthead at any time. To have your account and sites deleted,
          email <a href="mailto:hello@masthead.site">hello@masthead.site</a> from the account's
          address. Cancel any site licenses first; we don't refund the remaining period.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms. For significant changes, we email account holders at least
          30 days before they take effect. If you don't agree, you can close your account before
          then.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Law and disputes</h2>
        <p>
          Dutch law applies to these terms. Disputes go to the competent court in the
          Netherlands. If you are a consumer living elsewhere in the EU, you keep the protection
          of the mandatory rules of your country and can also bring a claim there.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <.marketing_footer current_user={assigns[:current_user]} />
</div>
